--- kps-S31aj VERIFIED CONCLUSIONS (owner's two questions answered) ---
Q1 "is the 1/7 universal (a theorem)?" -> NO. Sigma-k3/S3 is a MONOTONE-INCREASING function of k
   (0.027,0.087,0.130,0.113,0.143,0.201,0.260 for k=4..10) that CROSSES ~1/7 at k=8 FOR CONSEC ONLY
   (0.1428558 vs 1/7=0.1428571, off 1.3e-6). The ACTUAL k=8 binding minimizers {0,1,5,7,8,9,11,13},
   {1,5,7,8,9,11,12,13} give 0.245, 0.292 -- NOT near 1/7. Definitively a near-coincidence of the crossing.
Q2 "is the covariance-max robust?" -> YES, EXHAUSTIVELY. consec={0..7} MAXIMIZES Sigma-kappa_2 over ALL
   3432 bounded k=8 clusters (span<=14), 0 beaters. The cleanest provable target is EXHAUSTIVELY verified.
BONUS (the genuine structure): FERROMAGNETIC PHASE TRANSITION. Sigma-kappa_2(consec_k) sign-changes
   NEGATIVE(antiferro, k=3,4,5) -> POSITIVE(ferro, k>=6) at k=5->6 = mac-mini's n=5 compression boundary;
   peaks +0.772 at k=10. So the empty-sector correlations become FERROMAGNETIC (ordered phi^4 phase) at
   k=6, and consec is the ferromagnetic GROUND STATE (max order). The binding row k=8 sits in the ordered
   phase. 2002=C(14,5)=2*7*11*13 = the k=10 binding-row config count (THM-534) -- binomial config counts.
